  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Octopamine is a phenethylamine alkaloid that acts as a neurotransmitter and an alpha-adrenergic agonist with vasoconstrictor effects, and it has been classified as a cardiac stimulant among adrenergic agents. It remains an experimental drug and is not an established approved medicine in human therapy.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q424979&quot;>Wikidata Q424979</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>octopamine</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>C01CA18</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13251&quot;>DB13251</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/4581&quot;>4581</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:17134&quot;>17134</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q424979&quot;>Q424979</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C8H11NO2</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>153.181 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
